# deploy/p5/portal/catalogue/fields — the non-mode writable fields.
#
# EVERY entry here is intent, never mechanism (m9-portal-design.md §3). The
# reorder hold, target_ms, CAP_CLEAR, beta, ratchet internals, FEC and the
# autorate MAX are deliberately absent and must stay absent: exposing them makes
# the portal a back door for the invented constants OBJ-B exists to delete.
#
# There is also deliberately NO per-source participation field. ADR-003 §4 +
# OBJ-A: source participation is NATIVE (netifd metrics, set in GL's own GUI).
# An `/etc/bond/exclude` fact would be the `cell` mistake one layer up. Bar
# PC-4 asserts no field here writes a per-source fact.
#
# fields: key|kind|domain|consumer|label
#   kind     = enum | uint
#   domain   = enum -> space-separated literals
#              uint -> the name of the ENVELOPE file that declares the bounds.
#                      NOT a constant in this file. See `floor_kbit` below.
#   consumer = the artifact that READS the fact. `unbuilt` means the fact is
#              written per its own spec but nothing consumes it yet; the page
#              renders that plainly instead of implying the control works.
shape|enum|on off|unbuilt|Shaping (writes /etc/bond/shape per e4-shaping-in-dag.md:70; the E4 DAG consumer is U22, not built)
profile|enum|conservative balanced aggressive|unbuilt|Escalation profile -- risk appetite, not milliseconds. The mapping to bond-ecod's constants belongs INSIDE bond-ecod; the portal never names a constant.
# floor_kbit — the ONE numeric field the guardrail permits, and only because it
# is a REQUIREMENT (a service floor), not a measurement. INTENT.md OBJ-E /
# m9-portal-design.md §3.
#
# ITS UPPER BOUND IS AN OPEN QUESTION, NOT A NUMBER. "No arbitrary constants"
# applies to a validation range as hard as it applies to a rate. The only
# non-arbitrary ceiling is the autorate max OBJ-F derives from the summed
# per-source deliverable rate -- and OBJ-F is not built (U24). So the domain
# below names an ENVELOPE FILE the operator must declare; with no envelope on
# disk the field is rendered disabled with that reason and the CGI answers 400
# `no_envelope`. It is NOT given a placeholder ceiling.
# Lower bound is physics: a rate must be positive, so >= 1 kbit/s.
floor_kbit|uint|floor_envelope|unbuilt|Service floor (kbit/s) -- a REQUIREMENT. OBJ-F makes it yield when proven unachievable.
